// PIN: `@"path"` inside an argument list is not Koru syntax. The
// file-source closure only lives at step level (`name @"path"`).
// Before the fix the file-source marker scan mistook the `@"` inside the
// parens for a closure, ripped `print.ln(` away from its `)`, and died as
// "unbalanced parentheses"; the bare (host-line) form rode into backend
// Zig as an escaped-identifier token — the hole that let
// `std/guide:add(key) @"guides/x.md"}` ride into bench/airline_guides.k as
// residual include-ref prose. Desired: a frontend refusal naming the `@`.
~std/io:print.ln(@"guides/hold.payment-failed.md")
